{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The scale, massing and overall footprint of the proposed outbuilding would result in a dominant and disproportionate form of development within the rear garden, out of character with the prevailing built form of the area and of a size that fails to convincingly demonstrate ancillary use. This is notable given the sites location within the Becontree Estate. As such, this is considered contrary to:- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)- The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)-&nbsp;Policies SP2, SPP6, DMD1, DMD4 and DMD5 of&nbsp;the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The scale, footprint and height of the proposed outbuilding, particularly its depth and proximity to the boundary would result in an overbearing form of development that creates a sense of enclosure and visual dominance. The proposal would cause loss of outlook and overshadowing to the rear garden of the adjoining property no.649 Heathway, leading to a materially harmful impact on residential amenity.&nbsp;The proposal is therefore considered contrary to:- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);- The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012);- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD6 of&nbsp;the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
